{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ea7e39d99b57bc5a9d", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Work, Power and Energy - Test 2", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264161"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926411a", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264013", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3c"], "question": {"text": "A force $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{F}}=2 \\hat{i}+\\mathrm{b} \\hat{j}+\\hat{k}$ is applied on a particle and it undergoes a displacement $\\hat{i}-2 \\hat{j}-\\hat{k}$. What will be the value of $b$, if work done on the particle is zero."}, "options": [{"id": "58c810", "text": "0", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264014"}, {"id": "09918f", "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264015"}, {"id": "a7802f", "text": "2", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264016"}, {"id": "5849cb", "text": "$\\frac{1}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264017"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264018", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e85b3"], "question": {"text": "A boy is rolling a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>&nbsp;ball on the frictionless floor with the speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The ball gets deflected by an obstacle on the way. After deflection it moves with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of its initial kinetic energy. What is the speed of the ball now?"}, "options": [{"id": "ec3cbc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>19</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264019"}, {"id": "a39443", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926401a"}, {"id": "2dfdea", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>41</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926401b"}, {"id": "be37a1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>00</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926401c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926401d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["6117b9b867dbe2603c3ea8cc"], "concepts": ["6117b9d167dbe2603c3eaca6"], "question": {"text": "A body of $m \\mathrm{~kg}$ slides from rest along the curve of vertical circle from point $A$ to $B$ in friction less path. The velocity of the body at $B$ is:\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FogI6ALu6CRH_S1yuxN8XzJeJuZkm57N_XSBdZk0nDQ8.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br />$\\text { (given, } R=14 \\mathrm{~m}, g=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2 \\text { and } \\sqrt{2}=1.4 \\text { ) }$"}, "options": [{"id": "7cc8ae", "text": "$16.7 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926401e"}, {"id": "e390ec", "text": "$19.8 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926401f"}, {"id": "3b5547", "text": "$10.6 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264020"}, {"id": "7572bc", "text": "$21.9 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264021"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264022", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b68"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3f"], "question": {"text": "The ratio of powers of two motors is $\\dfrac{3\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{x}+1}$, that are capable of raising 300 kg water in 5 minutes and 50 kg water in 2 minutes respectively from a well of 100 m deep. The value of $x$ will be"}, "options": [{"id": "97bde4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264023"}, {"id": "c64906", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264024"}, {"id": "309e93", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264025"}, {"id": "36086b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264026"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264027", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["60e567aa499d1e49588f95c3"], "question": {"text": "A body of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> travels on straight line path with velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The net work done by the force during its displacement from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is"}, "options": [{"id": "d4bd09", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>64</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264028"}, {"id": "6be3c5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264029"}, {"id": "5a643a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926402a"}, {"id": "fc3e55", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>128</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926402b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926402c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f00"], "question": {"text": "A wedge of mass <math><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi></math> lies on a frictionless plane. A particle of mass <math><mi>m</mi></math> approaches the wedge with speed <math><mi>v</mi><mo>.</mo></math> There is no friction between the particle and the plane or between the particle and the wedge. The maximum height climbed by the particle on the wedge is given by:"}, "options": [{"id": "d31162", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926402d"}, {"id": "561b64", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926402e"}, {"id": "c6a87a", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926402f"}, {"id": "4e33b3", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264030"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264031", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b68"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b2b"], "question": {"text": "A body of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kg</mi></math> begins to move under the action of a time dependent force given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>→</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>t</mi><mo> </mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo> </mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>. The power developed by the force at the time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is given by:"}, "options": [{"id": "166642", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264032"}, {"id": "3ed117", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264033"}, {"id": "4a854c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264034"}, {"id": "0982b5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264035"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264036", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["6117b9b867dbe2603c3ea8cc"], "concepts": ["6117b9d167dbe2603c3eaca6"], "question": {"text": "A stone of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>, tied to a string is being whirled in a vertical circle with a uniform speed. The tension in the string is"}, "options": [{"id": "f722f4", "text": "the same throughout the motion.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264037"}, {"id": "5908a3", "text": "minimum when the rope is in the horizontal position.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264038"}, {"id": "c48883", "text": "minimum at the highest position of the circular path.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264039"}, {"id": "1b830f", "text": "minimum at the lowest position of the circular path.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926403a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926403b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e37"], "question": {"text": "A particle of charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> and mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is subjected to an electric field&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> in the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo></math>direction, where a and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> are constants. Initially the particle was at rest at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Other than the initial position the kinetic energy of the particle becomes zero when the distance of the particle from the origin is :"}, "options": [{"id": "524c82", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926403c"}, {"id": "bea72f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>&nbsp;", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926403d"}, {"id": "727b1f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926403e"}, {"id": "81c40f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926403f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264040", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["617aa9bdef3fe65ad8e80f6d"], "question": {"text": "<p>Identify the correct statements from the following:</p><p>(A) Work done by a man in lifting a bucket out of a well by means of a rope tied to the bucket is negative</p><p>(B) Work done by gravitational force in lifting a bucket out of a well by a rope tied to the bucket is negative</p><p>(C) Work done by friction on a body sliding down an inclined plane is positive</p><p>(D) Work done by an applied force on a body moving on a rough horizontal plane with uniform velocity is&nbsp;zero</p><p>(E) Work done by the air resistance on an oscillating pendulum is&nbsp;negative</p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "d36481", "text": "B and E only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264041"}, {"id": "4d4f45", "text": "A and C only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264042"}, {"id": "07f425", "text": "B, D and E only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264043"}, {"id": "99e529", "text": "B and D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264044"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264045", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b68"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87c4"], "question": {"text": "An automobile of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> accelerates starting from the origin and initially at rest, while the engine supplies constant power <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>. The position is given as a function of time by:"}, "options": [{"id": "67aa3e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><msup><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264046"}, {"id": "1e2a86", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><msup><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264047"}, {"id": "00ab16", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><msup><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264048"}, {"id": "b485f9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><msup><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264049"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926404a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["6117b9b867dbe2603c3ea8cc"], "concepts": ["6117b9d167dbe2603c3eaca6"], "question": {"text": "A bob of mass $m$ is suspended at a point $O$ by a light string of length $l$ and left to perform vertical motion (circular) as shown in figure. Initially, by applying horizontal velocity $v_0$ at the point ' A ', the string becomes slack when, the bob reaches at the point ' D '. The ratio of the kinetic energy of the bob at the points $B$ and $C$ is ______ -.\n\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F-ep44HFnumTncTOWFgZ7VUQO09feTJ99DK-y47b68HY.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>"}, "options": [{"id": "da63a5", "text": "1", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926404b"}, {"id": "8aae13", "text": "2", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926404c"}, {"id": "a62909", "text": "4", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926404d"}, {"id": "939bb2", "text": "3", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926404e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926404f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cac"], "question": {"text": "If the potential energy between two molecules is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>12</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math> then at equilibrium, separation between molecules, and the potential energy are:"}, "options": [{"id": "b488eb", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264050"}, {"id": "cd9fa0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264051"}, {"id": "3d61ac", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>B</mi></mrow><mi>A</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264052"}, {"id": "3a38bd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264053"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264054", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["6162fadf6ed13040ec8486fd"], "question": {"text": "<p>Arrange the four graphs in descending order of total work done; where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;are the work done corresponding to figure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> respectively.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fdd6c1e60-b6b0-4ca7-b87c-630d5cc81c08-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 139px;\" /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F27af9f55-ddf3-4d4a-a28e-fd5eac77a97b-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 136px;\" /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F08d1cdbc-29eb-4f38-9193-ab439a9b68b6-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 131px;\" /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fa34aed01-eb8d-4b85-bdff-95407cf42e72-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 127px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "6fe08c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264055"}, {"id": "c83e26", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264056"}, {"id": "78dee4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264057"}, {"id": "9b5d6e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264058"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264059", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b68"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b2b"], "question": {"text": "A body is moving unidirectionally under the influence of a constant power source. Its displacement in time $\\mathrm{t}$ is proportional to :"}, "options": [{"id": "de487d", "text": "$t$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926405a"}, {"id": "59a09e", "text": "$t^{3 / 2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926405b"}, {"id": "a73d16", "text": "$t^2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926405c"}, {"id": "6a2fdd", "text": "$t^{2 / 3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926405d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926405e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4721"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements: one is labelled as Assertion $\\mathbf{A}$ and the other is labelled as Reason $\\mathbf{R}$\nAssertion A: In a central force field, the work done is independent of the path chosen.\nReason R: Every force encountered in mechanics does not have an associated potential energy.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below"}, "options": [{"id": "6b605d", "text": "$\\mathbf{A}$ is false but $\\mathbf{R}$ is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926405f"}, {"id": "2d814b", "text": "Both $\\mathbf{A}$ and $\\mathbf{R}$ are true but $\\mathbf{R}$ is NOT the correct explanation of $\\mathbf{A}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264060"}, {"id": "bd9656", "text": "$\\mathbf{A}$ is true but $\\mathbf{R}$ is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264061"}, {"id": "4b1b06", "text": "Both $\\mathbf{A}$ and $\\mathbf{R}$ are true and $\\mathbf{R}$ is the correct explanation of $\\mathbf{A}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264062"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264063", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["60e567aa499d1e49588f95c3"], "question": {"text": "A body of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> dropped from a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;reaches the ground with a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></msqrt><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The value of work done&nbsp;by the air-friction is:"}, "options": [{"id": "0bca24", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>68</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264064"}, {"id": "12fea1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264065"}, {"id": "fb6586", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>64</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264066"}, {"id": "61940c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>64</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264067"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264068", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b68"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3f"], "question": {"text": "A <math><mn>60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> electric motor lifts an elevator having a maximum total load capacity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the frictional force on the elevator is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the speed of the elevator at full load is close to : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>HP</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>746</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "164a82", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1.7</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264069"}, {"id": "b8aa77", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1.9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926406a"}, {"id": "21f03d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1.5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926406b"}, {"id": "871db6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2.0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926406c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926406d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["6162fae16ed13040ec848803"], "question": {"text": "A body of mass $50 \\mathrm{~kg}$ is lifted to a height of $20 \\mathrm{~m}$ from the ground in the two different ways as shown in the figures. The ratio of work done against the gravity in both the respective cases, will be :\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FS-uVz1Dhc1SH2VTEV9EBncHPilM6gwiUmqP_AgakPLk.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "6ca3a8", "text": "$1: 2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926406e"}, {"id": "ef7810", "text": "$\\sqrt{3}: 2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926406f"}, {"id": "1ac143", "text": "$2: 1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264070"}, {"id": "06b32e", "text": "$1: 1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264071"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264072", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3c"], "question": {"text": "A block of mass 25 kg is pulled along a horizontal surface at a constant velocity by a force at an angle $45^{\\circ}$ with the horizontal. The friction coefficient between the block and the surface is 0.25. The work done by the pulling force for a displacement of 5 m of the block is:"}, "options": [{"id": "165564", "text": "970 J", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264073"}, {"id": "699bb5", "text": "735 J", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264074"}, {"id": "a7bb63", "text": "245 J", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264075"}, {"id": "f1c512", "text": "490 J", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264076"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:31.390Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:31.390Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926415f"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926415d", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264141", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["60e567aa499d1e49588f95c3"], "question": {"text": "A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is moving along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis under the action of force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>. The work done by the force in moving the block from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> will be _______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "7185b1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264142"}, {"id": "f5b07f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264143"}, {"id": "1c4500", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264144"}, {"id": "67604b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264145"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264146", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e85b3"], "question": {"text": "A block moving horizontally on a smooth surface with a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> splits into two equal parts. If one of the parts moves at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> in the same direction, then the fractional&nbsp;change in the kinetic energy will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;________."}, "options": [{"id": "a8e144", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264147"}, {"id": "4f37c8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264148"}, {"id": "0deaa0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264149"}, {"id": "6796eb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926414a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926414b", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["6117b9b867dbe2603c3ea8cc"], "concepts": ["617aa9bdef3fe65ad8e80f55"], "question": {"text": "A circular table is rotating with an angular velocity of $\\omega \\mathrm{rad} / \\mathrm{s}$ about its axis (see figure). There is a smooth groove along a radial direction on the table. A steel ball is gently placed at a distance of $1 \\mathrm{~m}$ on the groove. All the surfaces are smooth. If the radius of the table is $3 \\mathrm{~m}$, the radial velocity of the ball w.r.t. the table at the time ball leaves the table is $x \\sqrt{2} \\omega \\mathrm{m} / \\mathrm{s}$, where the value of $x$ is _____.\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F5jxdEQWJyDonHJm3ClguEqHfRU17MfS8aV9ZwgaHpe8.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "b23d1d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926414c"}, {"id": "82fce9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926414d"}, {"id": "7cb8b6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926414e"}, {"id": "9987bf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d926414f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264150", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b68"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87c4"], "question": {"text": "<p>To maintain a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> by a bus of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> on a plane rough road for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math> distance, the work done by the engine of the bus will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi></math>. [The coefficient of friction between tyre of bus and road is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>04</mn></math>]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "12faf9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264151"}, {"id": "833970", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264152"}, {"id": "df709e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264153"}, {"id": "5da66f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264154"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4b2ee0e063d9264155", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f00"], "question": {"text": "<p>A pendulum is suspended by a string of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The mass of the bob of the pendulum is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>. The bob is pulled aside until the string is at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with vertical as shown in the figure. After releasing the bob, the maximum velocity attained by the bob will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. (if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestora